<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29607" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">monstrātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		monstro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a shower, pointer out, introducer, inventor,
				teacher, informant</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aratri,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Triptolemus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacri iniqui,</span>”
				<i>an introducer of human sacrifices</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					399</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hospitii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. G.
					21</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Luc. 9, 979</span></i>.</div>
